n website errors, hosting settings and publishing problems.</p></article><article class="service"><span class="number">06</span><h3>Advanced IT</h3><p>Assess cloud access, network configuration and more complex technical issues before agreeing on the scope.</p></article></div></div></section><section class="block pricing"><div class="wrap"><h2>How remote help works</h2><div class="steps"><div><b>01</b><h3>Describe the issue</h3><p>Tell us what you are trying to accomplish, what device or software you use and what has gone wrong.</p></div><div><b>02</b><h3>Agree on a plan</h3><p>Confirm the appropriate specialty, rate and scope before starting a session.</p></div><div><b>03</b><h3>Work with a technician</h3><p>Follow guided steps or approve remote access when appropriate, and review the outcome together.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="block"><div class="wrap"><h2>Common questions</h2><div class="service-grid"><article class="service"><h3>Do we need a monthly contract?</h3><p>The planned model is pay-as-you-go, with the rate agreed before each session.</p></article><article class="service"><h3>Can you replace our managed IT provider?</h3><p>Hourly support is intended for defined tasks, not continuous monitoring, incident response or guaranteed uptime.</p></article><article class="service"><h3>Can you work with sensitive business data?</h3><p>Access requirements must be agreed first. Do not share regulated or confidential data until appropriate safeguards are established.</p></article></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href="/booking/">Explore booking</a><a class="plain" href="/#services">Other services</a></div></div></section></Base>